Title:
Nemesis — Native CLR Hooking Monitor for Reflective .NET Loads (AMSI/ETW Integrity + In-Memory PE Dumping)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Nemesis is a Windows runtime analysis tool aimed at common “bat → obfuscated PowerShell → C# stub → payload” loader chains (e.g., Jlaive/Crybat-style crypters). It creates a target process suspended, injects a monitoring DLL, and hooks CLR native load paths to detect reflective .NET assembly loads and dump the resulting PE images directly from memory. The tool also checks AMSI and ETW tampering by comparing live `amsi.dll`/`ntdll.dll` exports against on-disk copies, catching classic `AmsiScanBuffer`/`EtwEventWrite` patching and some CLR string-patching techniques. Output includes console + `%TEMP%\Nemesis.log` and dumped payloads in `%TEMP%\Nemesis_dumps`. It’s primarily useful for malware analysts and blue team researchers who need quick artifact extraction and telemetry from in-memory .NET loaders without relying on a full sandbox/EDR.

Technical Focus:
- Native-layer CLR hooking/detours (x64, MASM)
- CLR assembly load interception (`nLoadImage`, `nLoadFile`, `AssemblyNative::LoadFromBuffer`)
- Reflective loading detection and in-memory PE dumping
- AMSI/ETW bypass detection via export integrity checks (disk vs memory)
- Loader-chain runtime monitoring (BAT/PowerShell spawning and reinjection)

Use Cases:
- Dumping reflectively loaded .NET payloads from commodity crypter chains during detonation
- Identifying AMSI/ETW patching behavior in .NET stubs (RET patches, CLR string modifications)
- Rapid triage of suspicious `.bat`/PowerShell droppers on a lab VM to extract second-stage artifacts
- Building detections/IOCs based on observed CLR load paths and tamper patterns
- Reverse engineering Jlaive/ScrubCrypt-like ecosystems by capturing the “materialization” point of payloads

Keywords:
Windows, .NET, CLR, amsi.dll, ntdll.dll, AMSI, ETW, EtwEventWrite, AmsiScanBuffer, reflective loading, in-memory PE dump, process injection, suspended process, detours, MASM x64, AssemblyNative::LoadFromBuffer, nLoadImage, nLoadFile, Jlaive, Crybat, ScrubCrypt, malware analysis, loader chain, PowerShell, BAT dropper